7. Failure-Mode Register

7.1 HAP-Specific Failure Modes

ID Failure mode Trigger Detection Response
FM-H1 Proxy capture Agency proxy correlates with technological deployment, not agency Validation against held-out transition; correlation with deployment metrics Demote proxy, re-identify
FM-H2 Metric capture by normative framing Agency metric privileges one tradition without declaration Cross-tradition sensitivity review Scope clause enforcement
FM-H3 Non-identifiability masked Proxy reported as measurement absent identification audit Synthetic recovery gate; identification audit against HAP-2.1 Report as non-identifiable
FM-H4 Redundancy with \mathbf{V}(t) HAP produces no information beyond existing state Formal non-redundancy test; incremental explanatory power test Retire or reconceive HAP
FM-H5 Authority leakage HAP outputs used as political commands Evidence–decision boundary audit Firewall enforcement
FM-H6 Aggregation drift Scalar A_H introduced without justification Pre-registration review Revert to vector form
FM-H7 Circular reinforcement HAP findings depend on transition state used to define them Separability audit Restate as joint characterization

7.2 Operational Detection Procedures

FM-H1 detection protocol. Regress each agency proxy on a measure of technological deployment intensity (e.g., AI adoption rate) while controlling for the latent agency dimension. If the proxy's loading on deployment intensity exceeds 0.3 (on a standardized scale) and is statistically significant at the 1% level, the proxy is flagged for review.

FM-H3 detection protocol. Apply the synthetic recovery gate. If any parameter fails to meet the recovery criteria (bias > 10% or coverage < 90%), the dimension is flagged as potentially non-identifiable and subjected to a formal identification audit.

FM-H4 detection protocol. Conduct the incremental explanatory power test: regress a held-out agency outcome on \mathbf{V}, \mathbf{R}, and \mathcal{H}(t). If the HAP dimensions jointly add less than 5% incremental R^2, the non-redundancy proposition is not supported and HAP is flagged for reconception.

FM-H7 detection protocol. For each study, declare the separability structure (6.3). If \mathcal{H}_2 and \mathcal{H}_3 are both statistically indistinguishable from zero, the dimension is flagged as non-independent.

7.3 Revision Triggers

A revision of HAP is triggered by: (i) any FM-H1 through FM-H7 confirmed; (ii) new peer-reviewed evidence materially changing a prior; (iii) a confirmed structural break in an agency indicator series; or (iv) a HAP stress-test output that contradicts a standing assumption.

