Appendix C — Normalization and Aggregation Pipeline

C.1 Purpose

To define the full transformation from raw indicator to agency dimension and to composite constructions, including missing-data, zero-value, structural-break, and sensitivity handling.

C.2 Normalization Functions

Clipped min-max robust:

\tilde{x} = \text{clip}\!\left(\frac{x - x_{0.05}}{x_{0.95} - x_{0.05}},\ 0,\ 1\right)
\tag{C.1}

The 5th and 95th percentiles are computed on a frozen reference window \mathcal{R}_0 declared in the pre-registration. The window is never updated retroactively within a study.

Sigmoid normalization:

\tilde{x} = \sigma\!\left(\frac{x-\mu}{s}\right) = \frac{1}{1+e^{-(x-\mu)/s}}
\tag{C.2}

with \mu, s estimated on \mathcal{R}_0 and then frozen. A guard s > \epsilon_s is imposed.

Saturating threshold normalization:

\tilde{x} = \min\!\left(1,\ \frac{x}{x_{\text{ref}}}\right)
\tag{C.3}

with x_{\text{ref}} a declared physical or institutional reference value.

C.3 Zero-Value and Negative-Value Handling

For geometric aggregation we adopt the shifted form:

g_i = \exp\!\left(\frac{1}{n}\sum_{k=1}^{n} \ln\!\left(1 + \tilde{x}_{ik}\right)\right) - 1
\tag{C.4}

For indicators whose normalized support may become negative:

\tilde{x}' = \tilde{x} + c_0,\qquad c_0 = \max(0,\ -\min_i \tilde{x}_i) + \epsilon
\tag{C.5}

C.4 Weight Constraints

w_i \in [0,1],\qquad \sum_{i=1}^{n} w_i = 1.
\tag{C.6}

Weights are elicited by documented expert judgment and subjected to Dirichlet sensitivity analysis.

C.5 Missing-Data Policy

Missingness type Treatment
MCAR Multiple imputation, M=20 replicates, propagated into uncertainty
MAR Model-based imputation conditioned on observed covariates
MNAR Flagged; indicator demoted to candidate; excluded from headline
Structural absence Reported as an explicit gap; never imputed silently

C.6 Aggregation Modes (Secondary Constructions Only)

\mathcal{A}_{\text{geo}}(\mathcal{H},\mathbf{w}) = \exp\!\left(\sum_{i} w_i \ln(1+H_i)\right)-1
\tag{C.7}

\mathcal{A}_{\text{conc}}(\mathcal{H},\mathbf{w}) = \left(\sum_i w_i H_i^{\rho}\right)^{1/\rho},\quad \rho \in (0,1)
\tag{C.8}

\mathcal{A}_{\text{lin}}(\mathcal{H},\mathbf{w}) = \sum_i w_i H_i
\tag{C.9}

Rank stability across aggregation modes and across weight perturbations \mathbf{w} \sim \text{Dirichlet}(\mathbf{1}) is reported as the primary robustness statistic.

C.7 Sensitivity Design

Variance-based sensitivity uses Sobol' indices:

S_i = \frac{\mathbb{V}_{\mathbf{w}, \tilde{\mathbf{x}}}\!\left[\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{A}\mid w_i\right]\right]}{\mathbb{V}\!\left[\mathcal{A}\right]},
\qquad
S_{ij} = \frac{\mathbb{V}\!\left[\mathbb{E}\!\left[\mathcal{A}\mid w_i,w_j\right]\right]}{\mathbb{V}\!\left[\mathcal{A}\right]} - S_i - S_j
\tag{C.10}

estimated by a declared quasi-Monte Carlo design with a fixed seed in the pre-registration.

C.8 Structural-Break Handling

When a break is confirmed:

1. a revision proposal is filed;
2. the proposal is peer-reviewed;
3. if accepted, a new reference standard is issued with a new identifier;
4. both old and new series are published side by side for a transitional period.

