Appendix E — Contestation-Response Latency Calibration

E.1 Purpose

To specify the calibrated family of contestation-response latency functions, including parameter calibration against human-factors data, limiting behavior analysis, and alternative functional forms.

E.2 Primary Function

C_H(t) = I_H(t) \cdot \sigma\!\left(-\frac{\tau_{\text{system}}(t)}{\tau_{\text{human}}(t)} \cdot \alpha\right)
\tag{E.1}

Limiting behavior:

Condition C_H
\tau_{\text{system}} \gg \tau_{\text{human}}, I_H \to 0 0 (false gate)
\tau_{\text{system}} \ll \tau_{\text{human}}, I_H = 1 1 (genuine contestability)
I_H high, \tau_{\text{system}} \gg \tau_{\text{human}} I_H \cdot 0 = 0

E.3 Human Review Time Model

\tau_{\text{human}}(t) = \tau_{\text{base}} \cdot \left(1 + \frac{\kappa_1}{\text{expertise}(t)}\right) \cdot \left(1 + \frac{\kappa_2}{\text{interface\_quality}(t)}\right) \cdot \left(1 + \frac{\kappa_3}{\text{cognitive\_load}(t)}\right)
\tag{E.2}

Calibration values from human-factors literature:

Parameter Value / Range Source
\tau_{\text{base}} (co-located ToR) 5–15 seconds Reported in co-located takeover request studies
\tau_{\text{base}} (supervisory control) 52–59 seconds Decision-assessment task studies
Minimum safe takeover budget ~7 seconds Simulation studies
Optimal takeover budget 10 seconds Simulation studies
Full control resumption up to 40 seconds Driving simulation studies

Mean time-on-task in supervisory control tasks has been reported at approximately 52–59 seconds, substantially longer than the 5–15 second takeover times typically reported in co-located ToR studies . Studies have found that drivers typically experience a lag of 10 to 15 seconds between automation disengagement and resumption of control and may require up to 40 seconds to fully regain stable control .

E.4 Alternative Functional Forms

Threshold form:

C_H^{\text{thresh}}(t) = I_H(t) \cdot \mathbb{1}\!\left[\frac{\tau_{\text{system}}(t)}{\tau_{\text{human}}(t)} < \theta_C\right]
\tag{E.3}

Piecewise-linear form:

C_H^{\text{lin}}(t) = I_H(t) \cdot \max\!\left(0, 1 - \beta \cdot \frac{\tau_{\text{system}}(t)}{\tau_{\text{human}}(t)}\right)
\tag{E.4}

Survival-model form:

C_H^{\text{surv}}(t) = I_H(t) \cdot \exp\!\left(-\lambda_C \cdot \frac{\tau_{\text{system}}(t)}{\tau_{\text{human}}(t)}\right)
\tag{E.5}

Rank correlation across forms is reported alongside all published C_H values.

E.5 Blind-Accept Rate Operational Definition

\text{BAR}(t) = \frac{N_{\text{accepted without review}}}{N_{\text{total accepted}}}
\tag{E.6}

A review counts as substantive if any of the following conditions is met:

1. Review time exceeds \tau_{\text{review}} (declared per domain);
2. At least one edit or override attempt is made;
3. An independent evidence check is performed;
4. The reviewer documents a reason for disagreement before accepting.

E.6 Effective Oversight Composite

O_H(t) = w_1 \cdot (1 - \text{BAR}(t)) + w_2 \cdot \text{latency-to-intervention}(t) + w_3 \cdot (1 - \text{asymmetry\_penalty}(t))
\tag{E.7}

with w_1 + w_2 + w_3 = 1 declared in the pre-registration.

