J.3 Operational Detection Procedures

FM-H1 detection protocol. Regress each agency proxy on a measure of technological deployment intensity while controlling for the latent agency dimension. If the proxy's loading on deployment intensity exceeds 0.3 (standardized) and is statistically significant at the 1% level, the proxy is flagged.

FM-H3 detection protocol. Apply the synthetic recovery gate. If any parameter fails to meet the recovery criteria (bias > 10% or coverage < 90%), the dimension is flagged as potentially non-identifiable and subjected to a formal identification audit.

FM-H4 detection protocol. Regress a held-out agency outcome on \mathbf{V}, \mathbf{R}, and \mathcal{H}(t). If the HAP dimensions jointly add less than 5% incremental R^2, the non-redundancy proposition is not supported and HAP is flagged for reconception.

FM-H7 detection protocol. For each study, declare the separability structure (D.3). If \mathcal{H}_2 and \mathcal{H}_3 are both statistically indistinguishable from zero, the dimension is flagged as non-independent.

J.4 Revision Triggers

A revision of HAP is triggered by: (i) any FM-H1 through FM-H7 confirmed; (ii) new peer-reviewed evidence materially changing a prior; (iii) a confirmed structural break in an agency indicator series; or (iv) a HAP stress-test output that contradicts a standing assumption.

J.5 Revision Log

Every revision is logged with: identifier, date, trigger, proposal, reviewers, decision, and rollback point. The log is public.

