Appendix L — Collective Agency Specification

L.1 Purpose

To specify the collective agency dimension Col_H as a sensitivity case, including its measurement model, identification conditions, and relationship to individual agency dimensions.

L.2 Collective Agency Construct

Collective agency refers to a group's perceived ability to come together, establish common goals or shared interests, and take action to attain those goals. The Group-Related Collective Agency Scales (GCAS-23 and GCAS-12) provide validated instruments for measuring collective agency at the group level.

L.3 Measurement Model

Col^*_{it} = \boldsymbol{\beta}_{Col}^\top \mathbf{X}_t + \boldsymbol{\gamma}_{Col}^\top \mathbf{Z}_t + \varepsilon_{Col,it}
\tag{L.1}

A_{Col,jt} = \lambda_{Col,j} Col^*_{it} + \delta_{Col,jt}
\tag{L.2}

L.4 Identification Conditions

Collective agency has different identification conditions from individual agency:

1. Group-level data structure: indicators must be measured at the group level, not aggregated from individuals.
2. Within-group agreement: inter-rater agreement (e.g., r_{wg}) must exceed a declared threshold.
3. Group-level instruments: instruments must operate at the group level (e.g., group-level policy changes, collective bargaining rights).

L.5 Status Classification

Col_H is carried as a sensitivity case rather than a core dimension. When Col_H cannot be identified, it is reported as non-identifiable and quarantined from the core state vector. When it can be identified, it is reported alongside the core dimensions with a clear notation of its sensitivity-case status.

