Appendix O — Ethics and Dual-Use

O.1 Purpose

To specify the ethics review process, dual-use policy, and legal interfaces of HAP.

O.2 Ethics Review

Every HAP study undergoes ethics review addressing:

· human subjects (if any);
· privacy and DP budget adequacy;
· dual-use risk (O.3);
· potential misuse by state or corporate actors;
· whistleblower protection for internal dissent.

O.3 Dual-Use Policy

Tier Description Handling
Green No foreseeable harmful application Full publication
Amber Foreseeable harmful application under specific conditions Delayed publication with declared review
Red Directly enabling severe harm Internal-only; publication of the fact of restriction, not the content

The existence of Red-tier findings is disclosed; their content is not. This asymmetry is reviewed annually.

O.4 Legal Interfaces

HAP does not claim legal authority. It interfaces with:

· data-protection law (GDPR-equivalent regimes);
· export-control regimes;
· competition law;
· intellectual-property law;
· national-security review where applicable.

Where a legal constraint conflicts with a scientific obligation, the conflict is documented and the affected output is marked legally constrained.

O.5 Dissent and Whistleblower Protection

Internal dissent is recorded and preserved. Retaliation against dissenters is a governance breach. Whistleblower channels are independent of the Scientific Core.

